        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 150 adds support for the <a href=\"https://webaudio.github.io/web-speech-api/#dom-speechrecognitionoptions-quality\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">SpeechRecognitionOptions</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">quality</code> property</a>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136859632107520\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136859632107520</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds documentation for the <code class=\"notranslate\">quality</code> option.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44245",
            "title": "Technical review: Document the SpeechRecognition quality option",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-26T00:12:44.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-25T12:55:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 142 adds support for the SVG <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;a&gt;</code> element <a href=\"https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/linking.html#AElementDownloadAttribute\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">download</code> attribute</a>; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6265596395913216\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6265596395913216</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a proper reference page for the SVG <code class=\"notranslate\">download</code> attribute, and corrects relevant links to link to that rather than the HTML <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;a&gt;</code> page <code class=\"notranslate\">download</code> section.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
